{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"bottomStaff","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLPartSymbolV11bottomStaffAA14MXLStaffNumberVSgvp","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bottomStaff","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStaffNumber","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLStaffNumberV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol\/bottomstaff"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"bottomStaff","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffNumber","text":"MXLStaffNumber","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL14MXLStaffNumberV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"bottom-staff","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The staff number of the bottommost staff spanned by the symbol, used when the symbol does not extend across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the entire part.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol\/bottomStaff"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLPartSymbol":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The part-symbol type indicates how a symbol for a multi-staff part is indicated in the score; brace is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default value. The top-staff and bottom-staff attributes are used when the brace does not extend across the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire part. For example, in a 3-staff organ part, the top-staff will typically be 1 for the right hand, while"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the bottom-staff will typically be 2 for the left hand. Staff 3 for the pedals is usually outside the brace."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By default, the presence of a part-symbol element that does not extend across the entire part also indicates a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corresponding change in the common barlines within a part."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLPartSymbol","title":"MXLPartSymbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlpartsymbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLPartSymbol"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffNumber":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffNumber","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffNumber"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The staff-number type indicates staff numbers within a multi-staff part. Staves are numbered from top to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bottom, with 1 being the top staff on a part.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLStaffNumber","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffnumber","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffNumber"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, nor